{"parentUuid":"9966f5f6-5ab6-4f0f-b3d7-04ddda563d27","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UhCqVbnjkmQn4Z8SRpbrhL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VeriPB pseudo-boolean proof checker 2025 release PB-OPT optimization certificate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Pseudo Boolean Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - StephanGocht/VeriPB: Verifier for pseudo-Boolean proofs · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/StephanGocht/VeriPB\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2025 Markus Anders\",\"url\":\"https://jakobnordstrom.se/docs/publications/DocumentationVeriPBandCakePBforSATcompetition2025.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MIAO / Software / VeriPB · GitLab\",\"url\":\"https://gitlab.com/MIAOresearch/software/VeriPB\"},{\"title\":\"VERIPB and CAKEPB in the SAT Competition 2023\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"VeriPB Proof Checking Toolchain\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/veripb-proof-checking-toolchain\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization - Andy Oertel\",\"url\":\"https://aoertel.de/publications/2025-practically-feasible-proof-logging-for-pb/\"},{\"title\":\"Proof checker and pseudo-Boolean solver developed by WASP PhD excels at international conference | WASP\",\"url\":\"https://wasp-sweden.org/proof-checker-and-pseudo-boolean-solver-developed-by-wasp-phd-excels-at-international-conference/\"},{\"title\":\"PBLean: Pseudo-Boolean Proof Certificates for Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.08692v1\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, here's what I found about VeriPB and the 2025 release:\n\n## VeriPB 2025 Release\n\nVeriPB is a proof checker for verifying pseudo-Boolean certificates of satisfiability, unsatisfiability, and optimality bounds, and it was created on May 20, 2025.\n\n## Recent Developments with PB-OPT and Optimization\n\nAn efficient toolchain based on VeriPB and CakePB for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization has been presented, implementing proof logging for the full range of techniques in state-of-the-art solvers RoundingSat and Sat4j, including core-guided search and linear programming integration with Farkas certificates and cut generation.\n\n## Certification in Competitions\n\nWhen VeriPB cannot validate a proof within its time or memory limit, the corresponding instance is simply counted as OPT/UNSAT instead of certified OPT/UNSAT in the certified track. This relates directly to optimization certificate verification in the PB-OPT track mentioned in your query.\n\nVeriPB was described in the CP'25 paper \"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\".\n\nThe search results indicate active development and deployment of VeriPB in the 2025 competition season with support for optimization problem certification.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"98ee68f5-817c-483a-9adc-0c860dcbe83e","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:08.383Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9966f5f6-5ab6-4f0f-b3d7-04ddda563d27","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"04064b1f-772a-4d4f-92c2-d769000280cc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K88DaLup42oPVLzUWzoDDt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"anytime CP solver 2025 epsilon-optimal certificate Lecoutre Boussemart paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"[2302.05405] ACE, a generic constraint solver\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.05405\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] XCSP3-core: A Format for Representing Constraint Satisfaction/Optimization Problems | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/XCSP3-core:-A-Format-for-Representing-Constraint-Boussemart-Lecoutre/01e5286f0cb4ae6f76f9c8c95625e6302e131d71\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] XCSP3: An Integrated Format for Benchmarking Combinatorial Constrained Problems | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/XCSP3:-An-Integrated-Format-for-Benchmarking-Boussemart-Lecoutre/441e87ecb1f623cc3c57f076a99a7ffa010b1f14\"},{\"title\":\"MiniCP: a lightweight solver for constraint programming | Mathematical Programming Computation | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12532-020-00190-7\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Impact of Value Selection Heuristics in Scheduling Problems\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.27\"},{\"title\":\"Guiding Backtrack Search by Tracking Variables During Constraint Propagation\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2023.9\"},{\"title\":\"Disjunctive Scheduling in Tempo - DROPS - Schloss Dagstuhl\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.13\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Frédéric Boussemart\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pid/01/3426.html\"},{\"title\":\"About Benchmarking and Competitions of Solvers in Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"https://webusers.i3s.unice.fr/~malapert/publications/boussemart.ea-15-IPC.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found information related to the CP 2025 conference and work by Lecoutre and Boussemart, though the specific paper you're looking for with those exact keywords doesn't appear in the top results.\n\nThe search results show that the 31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025) has recently taken place, and there are several papers published in the LIPIcs proceedings for this conference.\n\nWhile the search didn't return a specific paper matching all your query terms (anytime CP solver 2025 epsilon-optimal certificate by Lecoutre and Boussemart), the results do show that:\n\n1. Various anytime extensions of A* have been proposed to compute a sequence of paths of increasing quality until finding an optimal path and proving its optimality, which relates to the anytime solver aspect of your query.\n\n2. Frédéric Boussemart and Christophe Lecoutre are well-known researchers in constraint programming who have published extensively together on constraint solvers and formats.\n\nIf you're looking for a specific 2025 paper on anytime solvers with epsilon-optimal certificates, you may want to check the full CP 2025 conference proceedings directly at the Schloss Dagstuhl website, or search for it on arXiv with more specific identifiers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5c214ce0-3e1a-4f16-bf2c-e0f4b1d87d64","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:08.601Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"04064b1f-772a-4d4f-92c2-d769000280cc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slu