{"parentUuid":"f1e9f4b7-b28e-4ec4-a32f-2c32b7a6dee3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BAribTfTZn1pjnr3CcGiTq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP 2025 SAT 2025 anytime certificate epsilon-optimal proof paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP 2025 Accepted Papers\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/accepted_papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"Pragmatics of SAT 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.pragmaticsofssat.org/2025/\"},{\"title\":\"CPP 2025 - POPL 2025 - conf.researchr.org\",\"url\":\"https://conf.researchr.org/home/POPL-2025/CPP-2025\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"2025 March SAT Version 1 | PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/840033474/2025-March-SAT-version-1\"},{\"title\":\"The SAT Competition - CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/competitions.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT 2025 - CFP\",\"url\":\"https://easychair.org/cfp/SAT2025\"},{\"title\":\"Workshops - CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/workshops.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CP 2025 and SAT 2025 conferences. The search returned information about accepted papers and conference details, but I didn't find a specific paper with the exact keywords \"anytime certificate epsilon-optimal proof\" in these results.\n\nCP 2025 is co-located with the 28th International Conference on Theory and Applications of Satisfiability Testing (SAT 2025). One of the accepted papers at CP 2025 is \"SLS-Enhanced Core-Boosted Linear Search for Anytime Maximum Satisfiability\" by Ole Lübke and Jeremias Berg, which relates to anytime algorithms for optimization problems.\n\nAdditionally, there is work on certifying solvers for combinatorial optimization, with a recent approach involving pseudo-Boolean proof logging, and a toolchain based on VeriPB and CakePB for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization.\n\nHowever, I was unable to locate a paper that specifically matches all the terms in your query (\"anytime certificate epsilon-optimal proof\"). If you're looking for a specific paper with these characteristics, you may want to check the full proceedings at the Dagstuhl repository or contact the conference organizers directly for more specific paper details.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"da8452ec-35e6-42a7-9e34-fd7107b6dd04","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:09.006Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1e9f4b7-b28e-4ec4-a32f-2c32b7a6dee3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"941d85a0-ee18-4da1-ac3a-9409e1a403cb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019He2uH9pKghpwi6SyBQiUF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PB Competition 2025 results pseudo-boolean solver track formats\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Pseudo Boolean Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/\"},{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PB25 Pseudo-Boolean Competition 2025 organized by Olivier Roussel,\",\"url\":\"https://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/slides/PB25.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[2501.03390] State-of-the-art Methods for Pseudo-Boolean Solving with SCIP\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.03390\"},{\"title\":\"Pseudo Boolean Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB24/\"},{\"title\":\"State-of-the-art Methods for Pseudo-Boolean Solving with SCIP\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2501.03390v1\"},{\"title\":\"The SAT Competition - CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/competitions.html\"},{\"title\":\"Proof checker and pseudo-Boolean solver developed by WASP PhD excels at international conference | WASP\",\"url\":\"https://wasp-sweden.org/proof-checker-and-pseudo-boolean-solver-developed-by-wasp-phd-excels-at-international-conference/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/output.html\"},{\"title\":\"AutoPBO: LLM-powered Optimization for Local Search PBO Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.04007\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about the PB Competition 2025 and the pseudo-boolean solver track formats:\n\n## PB25 Competition Overview\n\nThe 2025 pseudo-Boolean competition is organized as a special event of the SAT 2025 conference. It was organized by Olivier Roussel with a steering committee including Carlos Ansótegui, Johannes Fichte, and Jakob Nordström.\n\n## Participation Statistics\n\nThe competition had 18 solvers submitters and 3 benchmarks submitters, with 26 solvers (similar names and same authors), including 10 new solvers, and 67 different solver versions among which 6 were disqualified.\n\n## Track Formats\n\nFour tracks were opened unconditionally: PBS (PB Satisfaction) and PBO (PB Optimization) for linear constraints, with and without certificate of unsatisfiability/optimality.\n\nA new experimental \"parametric\" track was introduced to test solvers on parametric instances to identify how well they scale on specific series.\n\n## Results and Notable Features\n\nNot all UNSATISFIABLE and OPTIMUM FOUND answers could be checked and therefore some results should be taken with caution.\n\nRoundingSat was the only solver using the unchecked deletion mode of VeriPB.\n\nThe competition used VeriPB for proof validation and certification of solver results. The detailed results are available on the official PB25 website at https://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0de1e3c7-3d93-4f5a-b711-ad1b10f8fc01","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:09.325Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"941d85a0-ee18-4da1-ac3a-9409e1a403cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1d7bb8ea-d555-4923-919e-6f4ea31e7db9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Efq5PQGGbjro9VESkLripW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cake_lpr verified proof checker 2025 update pseudo-boolean\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7984575/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - tanyongkiam/cake_lpr: LPR proof checking with CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tanyongkiam/cake_lpr\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-72013-1_12\"},{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Verified LRAT and LPR Proof Checking with cake_lpr Yong Kiam Tan\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/cakelpr.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Verified Proof Checking\",\"url\":\"https://cakeml.org/checkers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2025 Markus Anders\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in ...\",\"url\":\"https://cakeml.org/tacas21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://research.chalmers.se/en/publication/531575\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/cake_lpr:-Verified-Propagation-Redundancy-Checking-Tan-Heule/a23f1afd3c101e136f810e2ceb74dad295aa2b6f\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about cake_lpr, the verified proof checker, and related 2025 updates:\n\n## cake_lpr Overview\n\ncake_lpr is a verified LPR proof checker developed in CakeML, designed to validate SAT solver proofs. The state-of-the-art proof system that allows for compact proof certificates is propagation redundancy (PR), and the LPR proof format is a new Linear PR format that extends the existing LRAT format with support for the addition of PR clauses.\n\n## Key Features\n\ncake_lpr is verified using CakeML's binary code extraction toolchain, which yields correctness guarantees for its machine code (binary) implementation. This is significant because unverified extraction and compilation tools are removed from its trusted computing base.\n\n## 2025 Updates\n\nAs of February 16, 2025, cake_lpr performance was improved by around 5-10% and its compiled binary size was reduced by around 20%.\n\n## Pseudo-Boolean Extension\n\nWhile the primary cake_lpr tool focuses on CNF unsatisfiability proofs, the broader ecosystem includes cake_pb, a family of tools and problem frontends for pseudo-Boolean proofs, with support for decision and optimization problems. Additionally, VeriPB and CakePB are verified pseudo-Boolean proof checkers mentioned in the SAT Competition 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8e7d4b62-6789-4ff2-b890-004a81de40a5","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:10.468Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1d7bb8ea-d555-4923-919e-6f4ea31e7db9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"aefb61c4-0475-4cc0-b825-31987412d349","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K558wvrZefnf2Qri26uWYi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"logic-based Benders decomposition anytime gap certificate 2025 industrial\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Enhanced logic-based Benders decomposition methods for the distributed heterogeneous non-permutation flow shop scheduling problem: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 63 , No 24 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207543.2025.2553820?mi=ik0enr\"},{\"title\":\"Critical-Path-Search Logic-Based Benders Decomposition Approaches for Flexible Job Shop Scheduling | INFORMS Journal on Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoo.2021.0056\"},{\"title\":\"Enhanced Logic-Based Benders Decomposition Approaches for Flexible Job Shop Scheduling Benchmark Problem with Discrete Operation Sequence Flexibility - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S100093452600074X\"},{\"title\":\"A Logic-Based Benders Decomposition Approach for Cyclic Microscopic Timetabling\",\"url\":\"https://tristan2025.org/proceedings/TRISTAN2025_ExtendedAbstract_337.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Nested logic-based Benders decomposition for disaster preparedness planning with horizontal coordination: IISE Transactions: Vol 58 , No 4 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/24725854.2025.2491495\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-030-54621-2_903-1\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2844846_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based Benders decomposition for bi-objective parallel machine selection and job scheduling with release dates and resource consumption - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054823003921\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/logic-based-benders-decomposition-lbbd-4e47b3ae-690a-44a4-9d80-a191b385b4e6\"},{\"title\":\"Planning and Scheduling by Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.1060.0371\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for \"logic-based Benders decomposition anytime gap certificate 2025 industrial\". Here are the key results:\n\n## Search Results Overview\n\nThe search returned several relevant academic papers and resources on logic-based Benders decomposition (LBBD) methods and their industrial applications:\n\n### Recent 2025 Publications:\n\n1. **Enhanced Logic-Based Benders Decomposition for Manufacturing** - A paper published September 10, 2025 in the International Journal of Production Research addresses the Distributed Heterogeneous Non-Permutation Flowshop Scheduling Problem (DHNPFSP), featuring advanced LBBD methods.\n\n2. **Nested Logic-Based Benders Decomposition** - A nested logic-based Benders decomposition algorithm with optimality and feasibility cuts was designed to solve disaster preparedness planning problems exactly, published in May 2025.\n\n3. **Flexible Job Shop Scheduling** - An LBBD framework was designed by integrating MILP and CP models to solve flexible job shop scheduling, and a hybrid method GA-CP was introduced to generate a tighter upper bound and accelerate LBBD convergence.\n\n### Key Industrial Applications:\n\nLogic-based Benders decomposition combines mixed-integer linear programming (MILP) and constraint programming (CP) to solve planning and scheduling problems, with tasks allocated to facilities using MILP and scheduled using CP.\n\nThe search results contain multiple recent papers on LBBD applications in manufacturing, scheduling, and logistics optimization, though specific papers directly addressing \"anytime gap certificates\" weren't prominently featured in these particular results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"48995397-c776-4108-832f-efc017f78915","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:11.172Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aefb61c4-0475-4cc0-b825-31987412d349","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
