{"parentUuid":"d01cf9fe-4685-4582-ba5f-7015b3577e69","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GHaXSQAGQWn3QvZvqsD9iu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01613RXW4CPhW1qsVjsGbtnD","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OR-Tools CP-SAT 2025 2026 anytime objective bound response_proto fill_tightened release notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8065,"cache_read_input_tokens":27336,"output_tokens":746,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8065},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":746,"cache_read_input_tokens":27336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8065,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cassjpo4nRvKDtS8eb5dB","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e905fd45-a7ec-47a2-9190-c806cf44f113","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:23.642Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d8ef93d4-281e-49f4-8852-b621bd60d01d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Esu73aTmsFEaVm4fmQXvr7","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP 2025 Accepted Papers on Anytime/Approximate Methods\n\nBased on the content provided, here is the relevant paper:\n\n**SLS-Enhanced Core-Boosted Linear Search for Anytime Maximum Satisfiability**\nOle Lübke and Jeremias Berg\n\nThis work addresses anytime MaxSAT solving through a hybrid approach combining stochastic local search with core-boosted techniques for progressively better solutions.\n\n---\n\n**Note:** Only one paper from the accepted papers list explicitly matches your specified topics. While other papers address optimization and constraint solving, they don't directly reference anytime methods, proof logging, bound certificates, or LBBD anytime approaches in their titles or descriptions provided."}]},"uuid":"d2643c0b-9e23-48c7-be95-c59434549a46","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:25.759Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d8ef93d4-281e-49f4-8852-b621bd60d01d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"affcec35-01df-4108-822d-25cbcee720d4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WwVWfrtkSGuoMLhuwV2svN","type":"tool_result","content":"# PB25 Competition Results & Track Information\n\n## 2025 Results\n\nThe competition concluded with results presented at SAT 2025. You can access:\n- **Overall results**: Available in [presentation slides](slides/PB25.pdf)\n- **Detailed PBS/PBO rankings**: [Results database](results/results.php?idev=115)\n- **WBO track rankings**: [Results database](results/results.php?idev=118)\n\nTop performers across tracks included solvers like Exact, PRINTEMPS, NaPS, and SCIP, though the webpage doesn't highlight a single \"best\" solver overall.\n\n## Available Tracks\n\nThe 2025 competition featured four unconditional tracks:\n- **PBS**: Pseudo-Boolean Satisfaction (decision track)\n- **PBO**: Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\n- Both tracks offered versions \"with and without certificate of unsatisfiability/optimality\" using VeriPB format\n\nA new **parametric scaling track** tested solver performance on problems like Pigeon Hole as difficulty increases, though this remained experimental.\n\n## Key Format & Format Changes\n\nThe webpage notes \"Globally, the PB25 competition will be organized as PB24.\" No specific dual-bound certificate track is mentioned. Regarding PBO format changes between years, the document states the format contains \"two new keywords\" introduced in PB24 but doesn't detail what changed for 2025 specifically over 2024."}]},"uuid":"5969a45b-b9b6-4b0e-a592-3bfbf71a0b71","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:26.259Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"affcec35-01df-4108-822d-25cbcee720d4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d01cf9fe-4685-4582-ba5f-7015b3577e69","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017eqhi6yD2bNQmnXrRRBJbp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"bound transfer\" cross instance dual bound \"constraint programming\" 2025 warm start\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP: Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=572\"},{\"title\":\"Initial values for the multipliers (warm start dual variables IPOPT) · Issue #88 · jump-dev/Ipopt.jl\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jump-dev/Ipopt.jl/issues/88\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning.\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/aaai/BessaDBRC25.html\"},{\"title\":\"Strengthening Dual Bounds for Multicommodity Capacitated Network Design with Unsplittable Flow Constraints – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2025/01/strengthening-dual-bounds-for-multicommodity-capacitated-network-design-with-unsplittable-flow-constraints/\"},{\"title\":\"[2408.12695] Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.12695\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming:\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/download/33208/35363\"},{\"title\":\"[2512.25018] Strengthening Dual Bounds for Multicommodity Capacitated Network Design with Unsplittable Flow Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.25018\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2408.12695\"},{\"title\":\"Warm Start of Mixed-Integer Programs for Model Predictive ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1910.08251\"},{\"title\":\"Warm-starting constraint generation for mixed-integer optimization:\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.13074\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query. Here are the results:\n\nThe search returned several relevant papers and resources related to dual bounds and constraint programming:\n\n1. **Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming (2025)**: A paper by Swann Bessa and colleagues on \"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning\" published at AAAI 2025.\n\n2. **Lagrangian Decomposition Methods**: Lagrangian decomposition is a relaxation method that provides dual bounds for constrained optimization problems by decomposing them into more manageable sub-problems, and these bounds can be used in branch-and-bound algorithms to prune the search space.\n\n3. **Network Design Problem**: Recent work on strengthening dual bounds for multicommodity capacitated network design focuses on introducing new classes of valid inequalities that can be implemented within solution approaches.\n\n4. **Warm Start in Optimization**: The search also returned results on warm-starting constraint generation for mixed-integer optimization problems, which relates to initializing solvers with prior knowledge from related problem instances.\n\nThe results include academic papers from 2024-2025 addressing dual bounds in constraint programming contexts, though the specific combination of all your search terms (bound transfer, cross-instance, warm start) may be covered within these papers' detailed content.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"94652b15-9cf1-45fc-8008-28ef26b39592","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:28.291Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d01cf9fe-4685-4582-ba5f-7015b3577e69","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
