\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"A practical introduction to Constraint Programming using CP-SAT and Python\",\"url\":\"https://pganalyze.com/blog/a-practical-introduction-to-constraint-programming-using-cp-sat\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I've found relevant information about the topics you mentioned in your query. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## OR-Tools CP-SAT Features\n\n**Response Proto and Objective Bounds:**\nA feasible solution has been found with a bound available to assess its quality via solver.best_objective_bound, and the search stops when the gap between the best feasible objective and the best objective bound is smaller than a limit, with both absolute and relative gap definitions available.\n\n**Fill Tightened Domains:**\nThe fill_tightened_domains_in_response parameter allows the solver to return tightened domains for variables when solving the feasibility version of a model. This can significantly reduce the search space, improving solver performance, especially when solving the model multiple times with different objectives or additional constraints. Enabling this parameter provides a list of tightened variable domains in the response object which you can then use in your model.\n\n**Recent Releases:**\nOR-Tools version 9.15.6755 was uploaded on January 14, 2026, with wheel packages available for various Python versions (3.10-3.14) and platforms.\n\nI was unable to find specific information about \"anytime objective\" as a named feature in the search results, though the CP-SAT solver does support intermediate solutions and bounds during solving. The official OR-Tools release notes page exists but didn't provide detailed 2025-2026 specific content in my search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c3f522e6-2d77-4eea-9945-31ca5cbf71df","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:33.682Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e905fd45-a7ec-47a2-9190-c806cf44f113","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
