{"parentUuid":"c07b999d-fd30-416f-b258-6c7bd2123dea","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ke8ZLBYtGxKJFDNChn4Brn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Drops Dagstuhl CP 2025 LIPIcs 21 proof logging pseudo-boolean optimization Oertel\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"Pseudo-Boolean Reasoning About States and Transitions to Certify Dynamic Programming and Decision Diagram Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2024.9\"},{\"title\":\"Practically feasible proof logging for pseudo-Boolean optimization | Lund University Publications\",\"url\":\"https://lup.lub.lu.se/search/publication/b5de3846-96d8-4689-874a-e0e3f939175c\"},{\"title\":\"Certified CNF Translations for Pseudo-Boolean Solving\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2022.16\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG (Short Paper)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42\"},{\"title\":\"A Multi-Stage Proof Logging Framework to Certify the Correctness of CP Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol307-cp2024/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization.\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pid/02/358.xml\"},{\"title\":\"Symmetric Core Learning for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization by ...\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/LIPIcs.CP.2025.15/LIPIcs.CP.2025.15.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of ...\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/LIPIcs.CP.2025.0/LIPIcs.CP.2025.0.pdf\"}]\n\nI found the paper you're looking for! Here's a summary of the search results:\n\nThe paper \"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\" by Wietze Koops, Daniel Le Berre, Magnus O. Myreen, Jakob Nordström, Andy Oertel, Yong Kiam Tan, and Marc Vinyals was published in the 31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025).\n\nThe paper addresses the challenge that certifying solvers have been standard for Boolean satisfiability (SAT), but developing similar tools for combinatorial optimization has remained difficult, with pseudo-Boolean proof logging being a recent promising approach that has mostly consisted of proof-of-concept works far from practical deployment.\n\nThe authors implement proof logging for the full range of techniques in the state-of-the-art solvers RoundingSat and Sat4j, including core-guided search and linear programming integration with Farkas certificates and cut generation, and their experimental evaluation shows that proof logging and checking performance in this paradigm is now quite close to the level of SAT solving.\n\nThe paper is published in Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), volume 340, article number 21 with supplementary material and software available from the RoundingSat repository.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"15eeff6e-8a86-475b-9ade-2ed20f3fc7c7","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:51.190Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c07b999d-fd30-416f-b258-6c7bd2123dea","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master",