{"parentUuid":"dc3bb349-e1cb-4372-abd7-99a31563764e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3356c51d9d10daab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WPvvtTRsV2Qu5KQuztZUfP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"three-stage\" OR \"multi-stage\" anytime decomposition time budget allocation 2025 OR 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Multi-Stage Decomposition and Hybrid Statistical Framework for Time Series Forecasting\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2075-1680/15/4/273\"},{\"title\":\"CORD: Co-design of Resource Allocation and Deadline ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.08484\"},{\"title\":\"Budget allocation problem for projects with considering risks, robustness, resiliency, and sustainability requirements - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2590123024010831\"},{\"title\":\"Budget Pacing: Complete Guide for Marketing Analysts (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://improvado.io/blog/budget-pacing\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal computing budget allocation - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optimal_computing_budget_allocation\"},{\"title\":\"Complexity of the Discrete Time-Cost Tradeoff Problem for Project Networks | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.45.2.302\"},{\"title\":\"hybrid-methods-for-resource-allocation-and-scheduling- ...\",\"url\":\"https://scispace.com/pdf/hybrid-methods-for-resource-allocation-and-scheduling-1vjcxcphw8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"2026 Digital Marketing Budget Allocation: Where to Invest for Maximum ROI | ALM Corp\",\"url\":\"https://almcorp.com/blog/2026-digital-marketing-budget-allocation-roi-guide/\"},{\"title\":\"st February 1 , 2026 Ministry of Finance Department of Economic Affairs\",\"url\":\"https://www.indiabudget.gov.in/doc/impbud2025-26.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A mathematical model for managing the multi-dimensional impacts of the COVID-19 pandemic in supply chain of a high-demand item | Annals of Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10479-022-04650-2\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I found one highly relevant article published in 2026 that matches your query:\n\nA novel three-stage hybrid statistical framework that systematically integrates multi-level signal decomposition with structured parametric modeling to enhance predictive accuracy was published in 2026. The proposed hybrid architectures—EMD–EEMD–ARIMA, EMD–EEMD–GMDH, and EMD–EEMD–ETS—employ a hierarchical decomposition–reconstruction strategy, with Empirical Mode Decomposition decomposing the observed series into intrinsic mode functions and a residual component in the first stage, and Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition applied in the second stage to further refine the extracted components.\n\nThe search results also returned several other relevant topics:\n- Deadline decomposition techniques that use static priority assignment computed offline to maximize parallelization\n- Optimal Computing Budget Allocation (OCBA), a simulation optimization method designed to maximize the Probability of Correct Selection while minimizing computational costs\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific information about \"anytime\" algorithms combined with time budget allocation in a three or multi-stage decomposition framework for 2025-2026. If you're looking for more specific research on anytime algorithms with time budget allocation, you may want to try a more targeted search focusing on anytime algorithms specifically.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7fa9dd09-3c87-4929-a0a2-7c4c9881ca72","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:52.742Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc3bb349-e1cb-4372-abd7-99a31563764e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-47